```julia
function casos_garantia_pendiente(P, pref0, Ep0, Bk0)
    # Busca una salida gastable de la clave 1 con valor >= 2.
    sp = [o for o in gastables_neg(Ep0, P, Bk0) if o.dueño == 1 && o.valor >= 2]
    isempty(sp) && return CasoNegativo[]
    o1 = sp[1]
    tip0 = last(pref0).id
    K = 2
    # V0: transferencia válida 1 brek a K
    slot0 = Ep0.fase == FasePoW ? 1 : Ep0.slot + 1
    k1 = 930000 + tip0
    V0 = gen_post(id = tip0 + 1, padre = tip0, slot = slot0, productor = 1, peso = 1,
                  sector = 0, txs = [tx_coinbase_post(3),
                                     tx_transferencia([o1.id],
                                        [salida_neg(k1, 1, K)], o1.dueño)])
    E0 = aplicar(Ep0, V0, P)
    E0 isa Err && return CasoNegativo[]
    # V1: depósito pendiente de K
    V1 = gen_post(id = V0.id + 1, padre = V0.id, slot = slot0 + 1, productor = 1,
                  peso = 1, sector = 0,
                  txs = [tx_coinbase_post(3), tx_deposito([k1], K, 1, K)])
    E1 = aplicar(E0, V1, P)
    E1 isa Err && return CasoNegativo[]
    # B: productor K sin garantía activa (solo el pendiente)
    B = gen_post(id = V1.id + 1, padre = V1.id, slot = slot0 + 2, productor = K,
                 peso = 1, sector = 0, txs = [tx_coinbase_post(3)])
    return [CasoNegativo("neg-garantia-deposito-pendiente", ErrGarantia,
                         "PoST", "Garantia", vcat(pref0, [V0, V1, B]))]
end
```
Wait: `E0 = aplicar(Ep0, V0, P)` — `Ep0` might be FasePoW (transition) or FasePoST. `aplicar` handles. Good. But `o1` must be spendable under V0's application phase. `gastables_neg` used Bk0's phase; if Bk0 is the transition block, phase PoST; V0 is also PoST at slot0. Good. For a later PoST block, also fine.

But careful: Bk0's slot might be Ep0.slot+1, and slot0 = Ep0.slot+1 too. Good. But if Bk0 is a PoW block? G2 only for PoST blocks, so Bk0.familia==PoST.

