`vencido_de`:
```julia
function vencido_de(E, g, slot, P)
    haskey(E.garantias, g) || return UInt64(0)
    v = Int128(0)
    for r in E.garantias[g].en_retirada
        r.inicio_slot + P.R_slots <= slot && (v += Int128(r.importe))
    end
    return v
end
```
But `tx_liberacion` importe is UInt64; `v+1` is Int128 → convert. `tx_liberacion(g, v+1, g)` calls `UInt64(importe)` — UInt64(Int128) works if nonneg. v+1 might exceed UInt64? no. Good. Actually `tx_liberacion(clave::Integer, importe::Integer, firmante::Integer)` does `UInt64(importe)`. Int128→UInt64 conversion works. Fine. But to be safe, `tx_liberacion(g, Int(v)+1, g)`.

